{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "Nifty 50 Weights: Calculate Index Component Influence",
  "scenario": "You're at a Mumbai equity desk reviewing the free-float market caps of 10 Nifty 50 constituents. Your PM asks: which stocks dominate the index, and what happens to the Nifty if Reliance drops 5% tomorrow? Build a weight calculator to answer it.",
  "instructions": "Calculate each stock's free-float market cap weight in the index, identify the top 3 heavyweights, and compute the index's sensitivity to a 5% Reliance move.",
  "learning_objective": "Calculate stock weights in a free-float market-cap weighted index and explain how heavyweight stocks disproportionately move the headline index level.",
  "hints": [
    "Weight formula is (Stock's Free-Float Market Cap / Total Free-Float Market Cap) × 100. Start by summing all free floats.",
    "After calculating weights, identify which three stocks have the largest weights — these are your heavyweights.",
    "Index sensitivity to Reliance: if Reliance is 12% of the index and falls 5%, the index falls roughly by Reliance_Weight × 5%."
  ],
